   138	## Owner flags (for a ruling)
   139	
   140	1. **Three markers** (above). I followed the launch instruction and composed nothing in the gaps.
   141	2. **The packet's "a hundred and fifty yards inside" is not on the page.** With the den under the floor's far lip (as the packet's site bullet and Movement 5's opening both have it), the six stand ten cords and half a floor inside the western line, and about two hundred yards from the nearest line to the east. I printed "From the middle of the floor it lay two hundred and twenty yards to the west, and they were standing on the wrong side of the floor from it." Movement 5's packet should take its distances from the manuscript.
   142	3. **The cord and the stride.** The protected figures do not close on one cord with a natural stride (ten cords = 220 yards gives a 22-yard cord; then twenty strides must make ten yards). So the cord's length and Karis's stride are never stated; only the six-and-a-half-foot offset is, which agrees with a cord of about sixty-five feet. If the owner wants the cord stated, it is one sentence in chapter 27.
   143	4. **"Three blank circles" against chapter 12.** Chapter 12 says that only at the bend does a road walk round a blank. I kept that true and added two blanks that no road goes round (one in hatching, one in water), found on a second reading and marked *guess*. They sit, loosely, where the Stair and the Hall will be; the hide is said not to take a straightedge, so nothing about an alignment is spent. If the plan wants the other two circles drawn later, cut one speech of Karis's (ch26:139–143).
   144	5. **The trials' order** is Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira, Oryn ("smallest first", since a burst is the loud thing), not the packet's listing order.
   145	6. **Additions to the trials:** Brom lifts the box inside ("Same."); Lira takes off the boot and asks along the line, northward; Seln's count of three. Lira's "I feel thirteen" (the year before her Kindling) is in chapter 30.
   146	7. **When the private tests fall:** after Oryn's crossings, in a quarter of an hour when the five are each occupied, a cord north of the stone at Brom's first turf. He prices the risk first (the hour; the quietest thing he owns; the ford's burst drew three). The Iron read is reopened once on the floor, "the same thing… done now for work, and he did not count it a third"; he writes only *No seam.*
   147	8. **Why he does not tell them** is mine: Lira's face after the step; and Oryn, who knows nothing of what he is, standing there ("that was not his alone to tell. It was a real reason. He distrusted it for coming so readily to hand."). He also takes it that the others suppose what he supposed until the stride: that a thing taken out of a Path stops where Paths stop. No one says so aloud.
   148	9. **The day-96 log has no deployment line**, for the first time since the shelf: "It would not have been true, and he did not yet know what would be." The logs of the 89th, 90th and 95th end on "Deployment since the Line: one."
   149	10. **The Ring's sheets are made on the 96th** (ten and a half), because nobody is inside the Ring again and Movement 5's packet does not stage them. Karis does not rub the band on the lip.
   150	11. **Cael overruns his own limit** by a quarter of an hour for the last two stones, and says so. It is the reason that six people are at the den at sunset.
   151	12. **Seln at the den:** "eight, or nine", all out to the east that morning, none back. Movement 5 has nine.
   152	13. **Karis's window** shows five rows and "a space at the foot of the leaf"; it says that she is frightened "by how well it agrees" and that she lifted her pencil from a sentence with *as though* in it. It gives no likeness, no who, no why.
   153	14. **Teague's window** has him read "HOLD" over five names without grudging it, and decide that "a feeling is not a figure". He is a silent witness on the 91st and does not nod.
   154	15. **The two HOLD slips are unresolved** at the movement's end. The ledger's board track gives the five no line for either, so the next packet should say that the fortnight ran out and Teague had them, or leave them be.
   155	16. **Seln and the stake's number:** he will not guess what thirty-one counts. Cael sets the stake beside the query in Ephram's letter and the posting as a third point: "He could rule the line now… What he could not do was say which way along it he was looking." Nobody says "Compact".
   156	17. **Vell's "session":** Cael says only "I know what she's speaking of. I don't know what she means by saying it now… It's hers… I only keep it."
   157	18. **Oryn "has been round it thirty times"** makes the Fallow road part of her ordinary round east of Thornwater. Her window in chapter 22 has the round take her "out by the far road"; I read that as the east road.
