   231	"So you'll all hear this, and you'll hear it once," said Oryn. "I'm coming in with you. I said I'd see him whole to the ninety-ninth, and I can't do that from a stone. But understand what you've got. If one of you puts a leg through something in there, I can pull it straight. I can splint it, and I can carry my end of you. I can't mend it. Not a scratch. Not till you're this side of that." She pointed at the stone with her chin. "Whatever happens in there happens to six people with no healer."
