    34	| Iron | Silver-grey | ~25% of active practitioners | Journeyman level; professional fighters, tradespeople |
    35	| Bronze | Warm gold | ~10% | Guild officers, minor academy graduates, respected figures |
    36	| Silver | Bright silver | ~4% | National-level respected; academy honors graduates |
    37	| Gold | Deep amber | <1% | Regional events; legendary status while living |
    38	| Platinum | White-blue | Historical figures only | No living Platinum holders as of Book 1 |
    39	| Void | Unknown | Mythological | Not confirmed to exist by the general population |
    40	
    41	Each tier contains ten ranks (Rank 1 through Rank 10). Rank 10 is the threshold for advancement to the next tier. Advancement requires both rank accumulation through use and a formal evaluation by a registered Arbiter station.
