    33	## Where we enter
    34	
    35	Oxhollow's bank at dusk on the 84th: a hundred and sixteen in hand, and six owed. Ribs taped, the calf bound, Lira's leg new and her right boot gone. Oryn is walking north; Teague's crew has crossed south. Nine days to Thornwater.
    36	
    37	## What this movement is for
    38	
    39	A contract written inside, a road the registry drew as nothing, and a line that stops every live Arbiter in the party while his already-dark Arbiter stays dark and his fragments answer. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4, B7] The mechanics are taught as trials before anything fights inside them. Turns and promises:
    40	
    41	- **Six days Oxhollow → Lowmarch (days 84–90), lightly on the page:** the ford walked quiet a day behind Teague's crew; Lira's carter's boot for two marks, packed with linen; the tape hated by noon; Brom keeps the healer's week to the hour and picks up the middle box with both hands on the eighth morning. A small physical problem on the road is optional and the author's.
    42	- **Lowmarch, day 90:** two hold slips with HOLD and **five names** ("Holds came to the ferry. Asked who. I said you."), waiting a fortnight or Teague. The traverse line read and priced: "Sixty-four's what the job was worth." / "Fair." **The posting under the stone's far edge**, the dust-curve on it, the hook-and-bar seal in wax; he reads it upside down, then gives it to Pike. Pike's face stops; Cael counts nine. "That's the Fallow Ring." / "That's quiet ground." **Pike's speech** (protected) and "You'll know. Your Arbiter tells you. It stops." Karis brings the page with two lines under it from the middle box: "A location. And a contract." The smith paid: a hundred and eight. Lira at the roof's edge: "Two hundred times. He counted." / "So do you. I've never once heard you say never."
    43	- **The board's room:** the wall rewritten, tenth; "Teague's nine up… He read that slip yesterday. Read it twice… I'd have done the same, and I told him, and he said he knew." **The council, once, in order:** Karis's case; Brom ("A survey kit's a cart's worth… That's not the reason. That's what it is."); Lira ("I'm saying it's a walk and a carry. I'm not saying it isn't the other thing."); Cael: "It pays."; **Seln reads the paper, not the words**: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside." / "It goes in." / "That's not a reason not to go." **The ninety-third**: nobody says *bring her*, and Karis writes "Thornwater, ninety-third. The healer." The Part-1 summary log (protected, "Twelve weeks").
    44	- **Day 91:** marked at the plank in front of eleven witnesses. The mail: **Ephram** and **Vell** (texts protected). **The void road (day 92):** the registry's printed sheet against the ground (seven dashed roads ending in white; this is the third); Karis's carter's map with three blank circles; "Their map has no roads. His has no quiet ground. Between them you get the country." Ephram's letter read at the wash at noon (Bracken told the registry "the Line and nothing past it"; Lira: "Good."). Vell's read at noon on the 94th, aloud, to Lira ("She puts the thing that decides it last." / "So does Ephram.").
    45	- **Thornwater, day 93:** Oryn on the bench at the gate with a carter's hand; "Fifteen days. Since the break." / "Breath stops at it." / "Ninth day. I said nine. You've counted." Her **two reasons** (a patient whole and still for the long reading; the carters' claim about a healer's hands, never checked); "You're a stop. I've added you… Don't make it a long stop." Her table that evening, seen from the loft door.
    46	- **Days 94–95, six on the Fallow road** (Oryn on the mule's down-slope side; the registry sheet goes back into the box at the east gate; past Thornwater's fork the printed sheet is white). **The rise:** he looks at the dark place where an Arbiter would be. Lira's hand up: "It's like the air got thick." Brom: "Like a door closing behind me." Oryn's hands half-raised and silent. Karis: "My Arbiter's gone." Seln: "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Five *backs* at one stride. The stone. **Cael felt nothing, either way, and says nothing**, for two reasons: he doesn't know what it means, and nobody asked. The log at the stone (protected). Camp on the road, no fire. The floor takes the last light like water, and Oryn holds her hands over the line until it's gone.
    47	- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch10 — OWNER-pending #48]
    48	- **The trials at the stone:** Lira's full burst becomes a step ("It's in me. It's not in the air."; the clock line); Brom's "Skin."; Karis sees every point and can fill none ("It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend."); Seln vanishes for a breath without his Path ("It was never most of what I do."); **Oryn's three crossings** with Brom's arm in her hands ("Nothing in my hands" / "A healer's hands stop working there."). **Cael's two private tests:** the Iron read released before the stride, running across it; at twenty strides a foot's worth of Wind evasion round a stone. From behind it is a man stepping. "It was dark before. It's dark now." Both halves true; together not the truth.
    49	- **Six over; the site catalogued** (eleven uprights broken at eleven heights; floor twenty-six strides; level under the cord; seamless under his palms, written only as "no seam"; the lip; Karis's chips don't match; the bands "None I own…"). **No instruments anywhere.** **The den** under the far lip (fresh prints; bones in one clause; scat; a hollow worn smooth). "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." Everyone looks at the line and the sun, then at Oryn, then at him. The log at the far lip (protected).
