+## 4. Standing defaults
+
+- **Calendar vocabulary:** no named season, month, month order or English weekday occurs. “Cold term,” “before the snow,” “fortnight,” frost and “time of year” are permitted season-blind language (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:51`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:5`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:15`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:146-150`).
+- **Units:** all measures are feet, yards, hands, strides, cords or paces; no metric unit occurs (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:11-19`; `manuscript/chapter-28.md:97-99,197-209`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:43-45,199-201`).
+- **Kindling counts and age:** there is no year count since Kindling. Lira's “year before my Kindling” identifies her remembered unkindled self and is not a count since it (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:147-151`). Cael remains eighteen; the prose does not state a conflicting age, and nineteen is reserved for day 102 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:395`; `BOOK_MAP.md:31,83`).
+- **Cael's canon outside protected text:** narration never says “his Path” or “Cael's Path,” never makes his Arbiter awake/working/unaffected, and never explains the fragments' answer. It says the Arbiter woke at Kindling and has been dark since the brass plate (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:165`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:185,219-229`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:257-279`). The two “his Path” uses concern Brom, not Cael (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:207-211`). The loose “mine” clauses occur only inside the two protected logs (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:237`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:225`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:154-157`).
+- **Quiet-ground defaults:** the five live Arbiters stop at the same step (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:189-227`); *Quieting* does not occur; “Compact” does not occur; no hound is seen; Oryn reads nobody inside; and Karis alone says “A circle is a made shape” of the place (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:169-177,197-217`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:193-227`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:155-197`).
+- **Reader Standard:** the prose is clear at thirteen-reader level; injuries have consequences without gore, moral concealment is named as concealment, and the den's bones are contained in one clause (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:223-229`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:289-297`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:171-175`; `BOOK_MAP.md:234`).
